{"tool_name":"pirs","contents":["biocontainers","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"pirs","identifiers":["doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/bts187"],"license":"GPL-2+","summary":"Profile based illumina pair-end reads simulator","home_url":"https://github.com/galaxy001/pirs","keywords":["Computer Simulation","High-Throughput Nucleotide Sequencing","Human Genome Project","Humans","Markov Chains","Sequence Analysis, DNA","Genomics"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":4889},"biotools":{"id":"pirs","home":"https://github.com/galaxy001/pirs","license":"GPL-2.0","summary":"pIRS is a program for simulating paired-end reads from a reference genome.  It\nis optimized for simulating reads similar to those generated from the Illumina\nplatform.","addition_date":"2022-03-23T17:56:34.867992Z","last_update_date":"2022-03-23T17:56:34.871438Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:pirs","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"name":"Fan Bai"},{"name":"Heng Li"},{"name":"Wei Fan"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Modelling and simulation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2426"}]}],"name":"pirs","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/bts187","metadata":{"abstract":"Motivation: The next-generation high-throughput sequencing technologies, especially from Illumina, have been widely used in re-sequencing and de novo assembly studies. However, there is no existing software that can simulate Illumina reads with real error and quality distributions and coverage bias yet, which is very useful in relevant software development and study designing of sequencing projects. Results: We provide a software package, pIRS (profile-based Illumina pair-end reads simulator), which simulates Illumina reads with empirical Base-Calling and GC%-depth profiles trained from real re-sequencing data. The error and 